---
import { localeFromPath } from '@portfolio/i18n';
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import LoanCalculator from '../../components/calculators/LoanCalculator';
---
<ToolLayout title="Auto loan calculator" description="Plan your next car with a little more clarity. Calculate a monthly payment or work backwards from the budget you have." category="Auto finance" image="auto" app>
  <LoanCalculator locale={localeFromPath(Astro.url.pathname)} kind="auto" client:load />
  <div slot="guide" class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="prose-copy"><h2>What will my monthly payment be?</h2><p>Enter the vehicle price, your down payment (enganche), any trade-in equity, the term, and your annual interest rate. The calculator finances the amount left after your down payment and trade-in.</p></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>How much car can I afford?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>Switch to purchasing power and enter your monthly budget. The calculator finds the loan principal that payment supports, then adds your cash down payment and trade-in—or calculates the purchase price from your down-payment percentage.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>A simulator, not a loan offer.</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>The 12% rate is an editable example, not a current lender quote. Payments assume fixed nominal annual interest divided into twelve monthly periods. Insurance, taxes, registration, and origination fees are excluded.</p><p>For a principal P, monthly rate r, and n months, payment = P × r ÷ (1 − (1 + r)⁻ⁿ). With zero interest, payment = P ÷ n. The final schedule payment adjusts for cent rounding.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolLayout>
